n, or rather cuz that's the gulling vvord betvveene the Cittizens vviues and their old dames, that man em to the garden; […] [W]hy ſiſter do you thinke I'le cunny-catch you, vvhen you are my cozen?","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["autistics and cousins","cater-cousin","country cousin","cous","coz","cuz","cousinal","cousincest","cousinfucker","cousinfucking","cousinhood","cousin humper","cousinize","Cousin John","cousinless","cousinlike","cousinliness","cousinly","cousin prime","cousinred","cousinry","cousins","cousinship","cousiny","cuzzy","everybody and his cousin","everybody and their cousin","everyone and his cousin","everyone and their cousin","false cousin"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cousin#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e29cba7cc913ef2785","definition":"A person who is swindled; a dupe.","example":"[I]f a plaine fellow well and cleanely apparelled, either in home-ſpun ruſſet or freeze (as the ſeaſon requires) with a five pouch at his girdle, happen to appeare in his ruſticall likenes: there is a Cozen ſaies one, At which word out flies the Taker, and thus giues the onſet vpon my olde Pennyfather.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["chump","chumpion","cousin","cull","cully","dupe","dotterel","easy mark","fall guy","fish","gudgeon","gull","juggins","live one","mark","mug","muggins","pigeon","rube","sap","saphead","schlemiel","sheep","simp","Simple Simon","soft touch","steamer","stiff","stooge","sucker"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["autistics and cousins","cater-cousin","country cousin","cous","coz","cuz","cousinal","cousincest","cousinfucker","cousinfucking","cousinhood","cousin humper","cousinize","Cousin John","cousinless","cousinlike","cousinliness","cousinly","cousin prime","cousinred","cousinry","cou